Z||000000||Alex4mula||08-10-2000||09:47 AM||||Last October my 98 C5 flooded with salty water when huricane Irene passed by my sister home. Because I have not been able to clean the title they are returning it to me and would not pay $500 they owed from the total payment. Water went up about 20". The computer is in the floor so I knmow it may screw up. The rest was new (17K mi). Do you think I can use that LS1 in a Fiero? Should I try to fix it and sell it? Should I sell it to a junker? Anyway I think I can get back the $500 plus the towing cost. What do you think??||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||08-10-2000||10:51 AM||||Let me get this straight...<P>You've got a totaled C-5 from 20" of salt water. Water got into the interior, but not the motor. Otherwise, the car is complete and your worried about getting $500 for it? <P>Ummm... send me a private email<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000002||Alex4mula||08-10-2000||11:04 AM||||Yeah yeah yeah. My wife gave me some hell because she knows it will be a nice project with LOTs of time away from her. I'm totally sure I can get more than the $500 I will loose. I just need reinforcement  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Anyway, as far as I know water did not got into the engine. It may need a new computer and a good cleaning inside after being 10 month in storage with that humidity there. I will try to go see it today. I don't want to spent $10K repairing it. If that the case I may take the engine (for a Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) and sell the rest to a yard. I I could repair it for let's say less than $3K then I may keep it or sell it. I think I'll have to subscribe to a Vette list then. I hope Archie to finish that LS1 kit soon if I keep the engine...||||reg||1
Z||000003||elfiero||08-10-2000||11:07 AM||||while it is possible to put that engine in<BR>a fiero,I wouldnt reccomend it unless you<BR>are firmiliar with fiero swaps and TPI swaps<BR>in particular.This one is about as hard as<BR>it gets.I know what i'm doing,I've done<BR>several different swaps into fieros.I believe<BR>archie is in process of creating a kit as we<BR>speak.Also,I am interested in buying the<BR>car the way it sits.Let me know how much you<BR>want for it.thanks<BR>bruce lee||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||08-10-2000||11:28 AM||||I'm familiar with swaps and mechanically/technically I may have no problem doing one of such. At the end still not sure what to do. I need to assess exactly how hard it could be to repair the C5. After that I will decide. I like the idea of a LS1 Fiero but not braking apart a nice repairable C5. Thanks for the buying offer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. Definitely I would have them in consideration if I decide to sell it.||||reg||1
